From d4ad96fa9f8a36f62c5d105d1cc057f75461691f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: albanread <albanread@googlemail.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 15:03:27 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Prose Display (S2): accelerant, app_server commit hook,
 desktop on S2

Accelerant.h: new optional hook B_COMMIT_RECTANGLES (0x500) with
commit_rectangles(const fill_rect_params*, uint32): app_server tells the
accelerant which frame buffer rectangles it has finished drawing, for
displays that present on demand.

app_server: AccelerantHWInterface fetches the hook and calls it from
_CopyBackToFront() (after the back-to-front copy) and _DrawCursor() (the
software cursor bypasses the back buffer). No behaviour change for
accelerants without the hook.

prose_display.accelerant: the frame buffer app_server draws into is the
device's surface pool itself, cloned from the driver (PRDS_CLONE_POOL keeps
the write-back memory type), so drawing is zero copy. The hook collects
rectangles (collapsing to a bounding box beyond 64) and a commit thread
sends them once per vsync, waiting on the retrace semaphore with a 20 ms
timeout so the desktop keeps updating when the host has no vsync (headless,
display asleep). Mode list: the host's preferred size plus the standard
modes up to the maximum surface; B_GET_PREFERRED_DISPLAY_MODE follows the
host window.

prose_display driver: ioctls for the accelerant (GET_SHARED_INFO,
GET_DEVICE_NAME, CLONE_POOL, SET_MODE with a display_mode, COMMIT with
up to 64 rects, ENABLE_EVENTS), B_GET_ACCELERANT_SIGNATURE, the boot
test pattern stops at first open, VSYNC releases the retrace semaphore
only for waiters (no runaway count), and the semaphore's owner becomes the
opener's team (user space may not acquire kernel-owned semaphores; it is
recreated when that team is gone).

Verified on VZ: the Haiku desktop with cursor renders through the S2
device; boot drawing coalesces to at most one commit per vsync, an idle
desktop commits ~4 times/s.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
